cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "MLFMM2HRTF"
abstract: >-
  Computation of individual head-related transfer functions (HRTFs) from a
  head mesh, up to 24 kHz, with a broadband multilevel fast multipole method
  (MLFMM) and the boundary element method (BEM): CHI formulation, adaptive
  octree, Ray and Diff sources, skin impedance. Python tools for mesh checks,
  source placement, direction grids, frequency interpolation, HRIR windowing,
  diffuse-field equalisation and SOFA export.
authors:
  - family-names: Langrenne
    given-names: Christophe
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-8065-5286"
    affiliation: "Laboratoire MACS, Conservatoire national des arts et métiers (Cnam), Paris, France"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/langrenne/MLFMM2HRTF"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-23
keywords:
  - HRTF
  - head-related transfer function
  - boundary element method
  - fast multipole method
  - MLFMM
  - SOFA
  - acoustics
